        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Furnishing fabric of woven silk, possibly made in Spain, 18th century"@en , "Furnishing fabric of woven silk. Buff ground with a floral pattern in pink, brick red, green, yellow and brown. There is a formal bunch of three flowers tied with a ribbon in the centre and other bunches tied on each side.\n\nLampas or tissue with gros de tours ground and the pattern bound in 3/1 twill. The colours are arranged in changes. Point repeat. Woven in coarse tabby. The material may have once formed part of a dress."@en ;
